      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part I, Line 2 - Grantmakers Explanation For Monitoring Use of Funds Outside US</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>SMALL AMOUNTS OF ASSISTANCE (I.E., FOOD, CLOTHING, HYGIENE ITEMS, MONEY, MEDICINE, AND MEDICAL CARE) ARE PROVIDED TO THE POOR ON AN INDIVIDUALIZED, PERSONAL BASIS BY ESEH AGENTS. SUCH CLOSE INTERACTION WITH THE RECIPIENTS OF THE ASSISTANCE ALLOWS FOR DAILY MONITORING OF THE USES OF THE ASSISTANCE PROVIDED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part I, Line 3f - Method of Accounting</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ESEH MAINTAINS DETAILED RECORDS OF ALL AMOUNTS EXPENDED ON A CASH BASIS. NONCASH ITEMS ARE VALUED USING A THRIFT SHOP VALUE FOR USED ITEMS (SUCH AS CLOTHING), AND PURCHASE VALUE FOR NEW ITEMS (SUCH AS FOOD). ADDITIONALLY, DETAILED RECORDS ARE MAINTAINED FOR THE RECIPIENTS, INCLUDING THEIR NAMES AND THE SPECIFIC ASSISTANCE PROVIDED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part III, Line 1 - Estimated Number of Recipients</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE NUMBER OF RECIPIENTS IS ESTIMATED BY THE ESEH AGENTS SERVING ON A DAILY BASIS IN THE VARIOUS MINISTRIES. FOR THE ACTIVITY "ASSIST POOR:MEDICAL,HOUSING,FOOD," ESTIMATES OF RECIPIENTS ARE MADE BASED ON THE NUMBER OF MEALS SERVED ANNUALLY, THE NUMBER OF DISPENSA BAGS DISTRIBUTED, THE NUMBER OF CANCER BEDS AVAILABLE, THE NUMBER OF NEEDY FAMILIES RECEIVING A SMALL STIPEND, ETC. FOR THE ACTIVITY "PRISON MINISTRY:FOOD,MED,SUPPL,BAIL," FOR THE ACTIVITY "PRISON OR MINISTRIES: TRAINING, ASSISTANCE," THE ESEH SISTERS SERVING THE SISTERS AND ASSOCIATES MINISTRIES PROVIDED THE NUMBER OF RECIPIENTS OF ASSISTANCE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
